acceptance:
The carry rule, in bin/lib/fm_context_pack.py only (`Store.brief` in fm_evidence.py stays exact; its tests in tests/lib/local_round_records.py:24-35 stay unchanged). In `build`, the exact lookup `store.brief(args.round, args.head)` runs first, unchanged. Only when it returns None, a new module-level function `carried_brief(store, root, round_number, head, base)` considers the authorized firstmate brief records for the same round (same filter as `Store.brief`: kind 'brief', `authorized is True`, actor 'firstmate', `round == round_number`; the store is already per project and task), newest first, and returns the first record whose head H1 satisfies every condition below for the round head H2 = `args.head`, else None:
(a) H1 != H2, both are 40-hex shas, and `git -C <root> merge-base --is-ancestor H1 H2` exits 0;
(b) the base ref B = `refs/remotes/origin/<base>` resolves in root (`git rev-parse --verify --quiet B^{commit}`); a missing base ref means no carry;
(c) `git -C <root> rev-list --no-merges H2 ^H1 ^B` prints nothing: every commit on the branch after H1 that the base does not already contain is a merge commit;
(d) with M1 = `git merge-base B H1` and M2 = `git merge-base B H2`, `fm_binding.change(root, H1, M1)` and `fm_binding.change(root, H2, M2)` (bin/lib/fm_binding.py:46-52) return the same `patch` (patch-id --stable) and the same `files` list.
Any git or binding error (ValueError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, a timeout) while checking a candidate rejects that candidate; it never raises out of `build`. A brief for a different round, an unauthorized brief, a brief written by any actor other than firstmate, or a head that differs from H1 by any non-merge commit, a rebase (H1 not an ancestor), or a merge that changes the task's patch or file list is never carried.

Tests, in tests/lib/context_pack_integration.py (run by tests/context-pack.test.sh; 152 lines today, stays under 1200), reusing its git fixture and `collect`, with a helper that builds: base commit on main, a branch commit H1 changing tests/feature.test.sh, `git update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main <main tip>`, a brief recorded for round 2 at H1 (remove the setUp fixture's round-2 brief at `self.head` first, as test_missing_stale_and_unauthorized_briefs_warn_without_blocking does), then:
(1) carry: main gains an unrelated commit (a new file outside tests/feature.test.sh), origin/main is updated to it, and H2 = `git merge --no-ff main` into the branch; `collect` with head H2 puts the brief text into the prompt before '# Context pack', the prompt contains `Written for head <H1>; carried to <H2>`, and no report gap contains 'missing authorized local brief';
(2) non-merge commit after H1 (H2 = H1 plus an ordinary commit): brief absent, gap ends with `non-merge commits follow it)`;
(3) evil merge (merge of main whose result also edits tests/feature.test.sh): brief absent, gap ends with `the task's change differs)`;
(4) rebase (H2 a new commit on main's tip with the same change, H1 not its ancestor): brief absent, gap ends with `it is not an ancestor of this head)`;
(5) the carry case with refs/remotes/origin/main deleted: brief absent, gap names the base ref as unavailable;
(6) the carry case with the brief recorded for round 1 instead of 2: brief absent and the gap text is exactly the old one (no candidate for this round);
(7) the carry case with the brief recorded `authorized=False`, and separately by actor 'worker-x': brief absent, MUST_NOT_REACH_PROMPT-style text never in the prompt.
Cases (1)-(5) are red on base (no carry exists, and the gap wording is new); (6) and (7) are regression guards, green on base and head. The existing test_missing_stale_and_unauthorized_briefs_warn_without_blocking stays unchanged and green: its 'b'*40 head is not a commit, so the candidate is rejected by an error and the substring check still holds. tests/lib/local_round_records.py is unchanged. A stub-free test is enough: the carry uses only local git, never gh.
